@*
    HR Policy (docs/03_PageBlueprints.md "Page — HR Policy"). Title/
    description/canonical/OG/AboutPage schema come from ViewData["Seo"] +
    ViewData["SeoPageType"], set in HrPolicyController.Index via
    ISeoService — see _Layout.cshtml's <head> and
    SeoStructuredDataViewComponent.

    Page flow (approved plan, 2026-08-03): Breadcrumb → Hero Banner
    (Standard, dedicated placeholder image — same "always has its own
    banner" precedent as About Us/Values) → HR Philosophy (Section Header +
    Image Block + copy, HrPhilosophyViewComponent) → Core Principles
    (Information Card Grid, CorePrinciplesViewComponent) → Employee
    Development (Section Header + Statistics Card + copy,
    EmployeeDevelopmentViewComponent). Career CTA is intentionally not
    reintroduced as a page-specific section — the global CTA Banner
    (_Layout.cshtml, docs/14_Decisions.md 2026-07-28) already renders on
    every page and the single-global-CTA architecture is kept as-is per
    project owner's approval. Social Media is likewise intentionally
    omitted, consistent with About Us/Our Values — the global Footer
    already covers it. Projects CTA / Partner Logos / Footer / Floating
    Contact Button are already global.
*@

@{
    var breadcrumbTrail = new List<AncinInsaat.ViewComponents.BreadcrumbItem>
    {
        new() { Label = "İnsan Kaynakları Politikası" }
    };
}
@await Component.InvokeAsync("Breadcrumb", new { trail = breadcrumbTrail })

@await Component.InvokeAsync("HeroBannerStandard", new
{
    heading = "İnsan Kaynakları Politikası",
    subheading = "Ancın İnşaat'ta insana değer veren, güvene dayalı bir kurum kültürü.",
    backgroundImageUrl = "/images/hero/hr-policy-placeholder.svg"
})

@await Component.InvokeAsync("HrPhilosophy")

@await Component.InvokeAsync("CorePrinciples")

@await Component.InvokeAsync("EmployeeDevelopment")
